    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0752" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg656"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Señor
                            Dupuy de Lome.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 346.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I had the honor to receive this
                    morning your note of yesterday’s date, informing me of the circumstances in
                    regard to the selection of a warehouse at Havana for the storage of the supplies
                    sent from this country for the relief of the needy in Cuba. I trust that the
                    arrangement now proposed will be entirely satisfactory, and that no further
                    delay will intervene to prevent the immediate reception and distribution of
                    these much needed contributions.</p>
                <p>In view of your statements, I have taken the liberty of correcting the erroneous
                    statements on the subject that have appeared in the press.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
